{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0013","billNumberShort":"H.B. 13","billNumberLong":"HB0013S01","fileNumber":"2026FL0227","shortTitle":"Municipal Services Fees and Political Subdivision Lien Amendments","currentSubVersion":"1","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"CUTLEP","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Cutler, Paul A.","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"HARPEWA","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Harper, Wayne A.","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill authorizes municipalities to place a political subdivision lien on property for certain past due services and makes related amendments.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>defines terms and modifies definitions;<hr><ltbullet>authorizes a municipality that sets a fee schedule by ordinance or resolution for water, sewer, or utility-related services provided by the municipality, to bill a customer receiving the water, sewer, or utility-related services;<hr><ltbullet>authorizes a municipality to place a political subdivision lien on property for certain past due service fees after providing notice of:<hr><ltbullet1>the past due fees; and<hr><ltbullet1>the municipality's intent to record a political subdivision lien if the past due fees remain unpaid;<hr><ltbullet>authorizes a municipality or special district to:<hr><ltbullet1>charge interest on a past due fee; and<hr><ltbullet1>charge and collect a one-time penalty on a past due fee as an administrative cost; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"RuthAnne Oakey-Frost","fiscalAnalyst":"Timothy Kevin Bereece","lastAction":"House/ filed","lastActionOwner":"House file for bills not passed","lastActionDate":"3/6/2026","trackingID":"WHNHQRHFSQ","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2025-12-02 14:54:41.510","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","vote